      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Based on the provided technical specs and prior art database, our draft summary for the USPTO could be as follows:\n\nAeroFlow Dynamics' turbine blade design utilizes a novel internal micro-channel cooling system incorporating a lattice structure for enhanced thermal dissipation, distinct from existing designs. Unlike prior art, which features standard cooling holes (US Patent 9,123,456) or external coatings for heat resistance (US Patents 11,222,333 and 10,456,789), the lattice structure featured in AeroFlow Dynamics' design demonstrates improved heat transfer and efficiency. This internal approach minimizes thermal resistance between the turbine blade and the cooling mechanism, ensuring greater overall performance and reduced energy consumption. By integrating a lattice structure within the micro-channel, AeroFlow Dynamics achieves a more comprehensive cooling solution, providing a significant novelty over existing solutions in the field.",
      "source": "target",
